@LBA2_PRODUCT_NAME@ @LBA2_VERSION_STRING_CONFIG@ - Nintendo Switch homebrew

INSTALL

Copy the switch/ folder from this package to the root of your SD card.
Launch switch/lba2cc/@LBA2_EXECUTABLE_NAME@.nro through the Homebrew Menu
in application mode (title takeover), not the Album applet.

GAME FILES

This source port does not include Little Big Adventure 2 game files.
Copy your legally owned retail installation's data to:

    sdmc:/lba2/

LBA2.HQR and the other HQR files go directly inside lba2/. Preserve the
Music/, VIDEO/ and VOX/ subfolders from your installation, including their
contents. No extra data/ folder is needed.

SAVES, SETTINGS AND LOGS

Writable files live in sdmc:/switch/lba2cc/user/, separately from game data.
Back up this folder before replacing the application. Existing controller
save handling generates names automatically; no keyboard is required.

CONTROLS AND EXIT

Use the existing gamepad controls with attached Joy-Cons, a Joy-Con pair,
or a Pro Controller. Single sideways Joy-Con play is not a supported target.
Use the game's Quit option to save settings and return to the Homebrew Menu.

STATUS

This is an initial homebrew port. A successful build does not certify
hardware compatibility. Verify boot, menus, gameplay, save/load, music,
speech, movies, dock/undock, sleep/wake and clean exit on a real console.

DEBUGGING AND LICENSE

The separate debug/ folder contains the unstripped ELF for debugging; it
does not need to be copied to the SD card. Logs are in user/adeline.log.
The engine is distributed under GPL v2; see LICENSE. SDL2 and devkitPro's
Switch libraries provide the platform support. The source is available at:
https://github.com/LBALab/lba2-classic-community
